{
  "id": "ss.relic.numb",
  "name": "Numbing sting",
  "description": "A wasp's sting run out from the point of a banded amber abdomen — a fat teardrop at the top left with three dark bands across it — a pale curved needle, thick at the root and drawn to nothing at the point, lower edge in shadow — with two frost-blue arcs standing off its point down to the right, the near one tighter and paler. The arcs are ring segments with ring outlines under them, never filled discs, so they are ripples of cold going out ahead of the sting and not beads sitting on it. Every hit slows for a second; the sting is the hit, and the cold arcs are the second. The abdomen is the only body there is, so there is no face, and the bands are what say wasp rather than the ball-and-tube of ss.relic.feed; the sting does not fork, which keeps it apart from the horn of ss.relic.ram.",
